«
@@ ============================================================
@@ MCPropagate — propagation of uncertainty by the Monte Carlo
@@ method (GUM Supplement 1, JCGM 101:2008).
@@
@@ Input:  F Vars Vals M
@@   F     the model: an expression of the names in Vars, or a
@@         program that takes one value per input from the stack;
@@   Vars  the list of the input names, e.g. { a b };
@@   Vals  the list of the inputs, in the same order. The type of
@@         each one tells its distribution:
@@           10±σ1    normal, mean 10, standard deviation 1;
@@           9…11     rectangular between 9 and 11 (also 10±1
@@                    and 10±10%);
@@           « … »    a program that returns one draw, for instance
@@                    « 10 1 ⓁLgNrmRand », for any distribution;
@@           10       an exact value.
@@         Inputs may carry units.
@@   M     the number of draws; 0 lets the program stop by itself
@@         when the result is stable to two significant digits of
@@         the uncertainty, after at most 20 000 draws or one minute.
@@ Output: the number of draws used, tagged "N";
@@         the 95 % coverage interval, probabilistically symmetric
@@         (2.5 % of the draws on each side), tagged "95%";
@@         the mean and standard deviation of the draws, Y±σu.
@@ Correlations: none, unless a global variable ρij holds one
@@ coefficient for all the pairs or the full correlation matrix, in
@@ the order of Vals, as for σRFxjxi. Normal inputs are then
@@ correlated exactly (Cholesky factor of ρij), inputs given by
@@ bounds through a Gaussian copula; a program input cannot be.
@@ Method: a program specialized for
@@ the model is compiled once, then run by batches. The normal
@@ draws use the polar method, which needs no angle mode.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  "" "" { }
  → mdl vn vl ndr dcl drw prm
  «
    @ One declaration, one draw recipe and three parameters per input
    1 vl Size For i
      vl i Get 0
      → v un
      «
        If 'v' Rcl TypeName "unit" == Then
          1 v →Unit 'un' Store
          v UVal 'v' Store
        End
        'v' Rcl TypeName i →Text
        → tn ix
        «
          dcl " mcA" + ix + " mcB" + ix + " mcU" + ix + 'dcl' Store
          Case
            tn "uncertain" == Then
              v Explode
              drw " 0 0 2 Do Drop Drop Drop Rand 2 * 1 - Rand 2 * 1 - Dup2 Sq Swap Sq + Until Dup 1 < Over 0 > And End Dup Ln -2 * Swap / √ Swap Drop * mcB" +
              ix + " * mcA" + ix + " +" + 'drw' Store
            End
            tn "range" == Then
              v Explode Over -
              drw " Rand mcB" + ix + " * mcA" + ix + " +" + 'drw' Store
            End
            tn "drange" == Then
              v Explode → cv dv « cv dv - 2 dv * »
              drw " Rand mcB" + ix + " * mcA" + ix + " +" + 'drw' Store
            End
            tn "prange" == Then
              v Explode → cv pv « cv Abs pv * 100 / → dv « cv dv - 2 dv * » »
              drw " Rand mcB" + ix + " * mcA" + ix + " +" + 'drw' Store
            End
            tn "program" == Then
              'v' Rcl 0
              drw " mcA" + ix + 'drw' Store
            End
            v 0
            drw " mcA" + ix + 'drw' Store
          End
          If un TypeName "unit" == Then
            drw " mcU" + ix + " *" + 'drw' Store
          End
          2 →List prm Swap + un + 'prm' Store
        »
      »
    Next

    @ Correlations: a global variable ρij, as for σRFxjxi, holds one
    @ coefficient for all the pairs or the full correlation matrix. Then
    @ each draw takes n independent normal variates z, forms w = L·z with
    @ L the Cholesky factor of ρij, and gives a±σb inputs a + b·wᵢ and
    @ bounded inputs a + (b − a)·Φ(wᵢ) (Gaussian copula)
    IfErr 'ρij' Rcl Then Drop 0 End
    vl Size
    → mcr nvi
    «
      @ The absolute value of a matrix is its norm, never 0 for ρij
      If mcr Abs 0 ≠ nvi 1 > And Then
        @ The full matrix, from one coefficient if needed
        If mcr TypeName "array" == Then
          If mcr Size 1 Get nvi ≠ Then
            "MCPropagate: the size of ρij differs from the number of inputs" DoError
          End
          1 nvi For iq 1 nvi For kc
            If mcr { } iq + kc + Get mcr { } kc + iq + Get - Abs 1E-9 > Then
              "MCPropagate: ρij is not symmetric" DoError
            End
          Next Next
          mcr
        Else
          If mcr 1 > mcr -1 nvi 1 - / 1E-12 - < Or Then
            "MCPropagate: ρij is outside −1/(n−1)…1 for n inputs" DoError
          End
          { } nvi + nvi + mcr Con
          1 nvi For iq { } iq + iq + 1 Put Next
        End
        → rmx
        «
          @ An input given by a program draws by itself: it cannot be correlated
          1 nvi For iq
            vl iq Get
            If Dup TypeName "unit" == Then UVal End
            If TypeName "program" == Then
              1 nvi For kc
                If kc iq ≠ Then
                  If rmx { } iq + kc + Get Abs 1E-12 > Then
                    "MCPropagate: a correlated input must be a±σb or bounds" DoError
                  End
                End
              Next
            End
          Next
          @ Cholesky factor L of ρij; a negative pivot means that some
          @ combination of the inputs would have a negative variance
          { } nvi + nvi + 0 Con
          → chl
          «
            1 nvi For j
              rmx { } j + j + Get
              If j 1 > Then 1 j 1 - For kc chl { } j + kc + Get Sq - Next End
              If Dup -1E-9 < Then "MCPropagate: ρij is not a valid correlation matrix" DoError End
              0 Max √
              → ljj
              «
                chl { } j + j + ljj Put 'chl' Store
                If j nvi < Then
                  j 1 + nvi For iq
                    rmx { } iq + j + Get
                    If j 1 > Then
                      1 j 1 - For kc chl { } iq + kc + Get chl { } j + kc + Get * - Next
                    End
                    If ljj 1E-9 > Then
                      ljj / chl { } iq + j + 3 Roll Put 'chl' Store
                    Else
                      If Abs 1E-9 > Then "MCPropagate: ρij is not a valid correlation matrix" DoError End
                    End
                  Next
                End
              »
            Next
            @ The draw recipe, rebuilt: n normal variates, w = L·z, then each input
            ""
            1 nvi For iq
              " 0 0 2 Do Drop Drop Drop Rand 2 * 1 - Rand 2 * 1 - Dup2 Sq Swap Sq + Until Dup 1 < Over 0 > And End Dup Ln -2 * Swap / √ Swap Drop *" +
            Next
            " " + nvi →Text + " →Array mcL Swap * → mcZ «" +
            1 nvi For iq
              iq →Text
              vl iq Get
              → ix vq
              «
                vq If Dup TypeName "unit" == Then UVal End TypeName
                → tq
                «
                  Case
                    tq "uncertain" == Then
                      " mcZ " + ix + " Get mcB" + ix + " * mcA" + ix + " +" +
                    End
                    tq "range" == tq "drange" == Or tq "prange" == Or Then
                      " 0 1 mcZ " + ix + " Get UTPN Neg 1 + mcB" + ix + " * mcA" + ix + " +" +
                    End
                    " mcA" + ix +
                  End
                  If vq TypeName "unit" == Then " mcU" + ix + " *" + End
                »
              »
            Next
            " »" + 'drw' Store
            dcl " mcL" + 'dcl' Store
            prm chl 1 →List + 'prm' Store
          »
        »
      End
    »

    @ The evaluation of the model on one set of draws
    If 'mdl' Rcl TypeName "program" == Then
      " mcF"
    Else
      vn →Text Dup Size 2 - 3 Swap Sub
      @ The text of the model, to compile it with the inputs as local
      @ variables: the fast path. A constant loses its marker in the text;
      @ when the text does not read back as the model, substitute instead
      'mdl' Rcl →Text 0
      → nms tx okf
      «
        IfErr tx Compile 'mdl' Rcl Same 'okf' Store Then End
        If okf Then
          " → " nms + " « " + tx + " →Num »" +
        Else
          " " vn Size →Text + " →List → mcV « mcF { } 1 " + vn Size →Text +
          " For mcI mcW mcI Get + mcV mcI Get + Next Where →Num »" +
        End
      »
    End
    → ev
    «
      @ A first compiled program without unit conversion, for one probe
      "« →" dcl + " mcF mcW mcY mcN « 1 mcN Start" + drw + ev + " Next » »" + Compile
      → pg0
      «
        prm List→ Drop 'mdl' Rcl vn 1 1 pg0
        → y0
        «
          If y0 TypeName → tn « tn "expression" == tn "symbol" == Or » Then
            "MCPropagate: the model does not give a number" DoError
          End
          0 'pg0' Rcl
          If y0 TypeName "unit" == Then
            Drop Drop
            1 y0 →Unit
            "« →" dcl + " mcF mcW mcY mcN « 1 mcN Start" + drw + ev + " mcY Convert UVal Next » »" + Compile
          End
          { } 0 0 0 0  0 0 0 0
          y0 If Dup TypeName "unit" == Then UVal End
          Ticks
          → yu pg all nn ymn sdv done s1 s2 s3 s4 yrf tk0
          «
            Do
              If ndr 0 > Then ndr nn - 500 Min Else 500 End
              → nb
              «
                prm List→ Drop 'mdl' Rcl vn yu nb pg
                nb →List
                Dup all Swap + 'all' Store
                @ Running sums of the powers of the draws, less a reference
                « yrf - » Map
                → dl
                «
                  dl ΣList 's1' Store+
                  dl « Sq » Map ΣList 's2' Store+
                  dl « Dup Sq * » Map ΣList 's3' Store+
                  dl « Sq Sq » Map ΣList 's4' Store+
                »
                nn nb + 'nn' Store
              »
              s1 nn / yrf + 'ymn' Store
              If nn 1 > Then
                s2 s1 Sq nn / - nn 1 - / 0 Max √ 'sdv' Store
              End
              If ndr 0 > Then
                If nn ndr ≥ Then 1 'done' Store End
              Else
                If sdv 0 == nn 20000 ≥ Or Ticks tk0 - 60000 > Or Then
                  1 'done' Store
                Else
                  If nn 1000 ≥ Then
                    @ Kurtosis from the running sums, on the stack only
                    s4 nn / s1 nn / 4 * s3 * nn / - s1 nn / Sq 6 * s2 * nn / + s1 nn / Sq Sq 3 * -
                    s2 nn / s1 nn / Sq - Sq /
                    @ Standard errors of the mean and of the standard deviation;
                    @ no local block here: one inside this loop corrupts objects
                    @ when memory is short
                    1 - 4 nn * / √ sdv *
                    sdv nn √ / Max 2 *
                    0.5 10 sdv Log10 Floor 1 - ^ *
                    If ≤ Then 1 'done' Store End
                  End
                End
              End
            Until done End

            all Sort
            → srt
            «
              nn "N" →Tag
              srt 0.025 nn * 0.5 + IP 1 Max Get
              srt 0.975 nn * 0.5 + IP nn Min Get
              →Range
              If yu TypeName "unit" == Then yu →Unit End
              "95%" →Tag
              ymn sdv →σRange
              If yu TypeName "unit" == Then yu →Unit End
            »
          »
        »
      »
    »
  »
»
